From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] compstui: the whole of CPSUI -- groups, inserted pages, option lists, results

Printer drivers' preferences and properties are built through CPSUI: the
driver's DrvDocumentPropertySheets and DrvDevicePropertySheets (and its
plug-ins) call ComPropSheet to add pages, groups, other PFNPROPSHEETUI
functions and COMPROPSHEETUI option lists that CPSUI shows. Ours knew
only how to add plain pages; makers' sheets stopped at the first other
call (Brother's at CPSFUNC_INSERT_PSUIPAGE, so it showed nothing). Now,
from the compstui.h reference:

- A sheet is a tree of groups and pages: a PFNPROPSHEETUI function gets a
  group handle of its own, CPSFUNC_INSERT_PSUIPAGE inserts any kind of
  pages (a group parent, a COMPROPSHEETUI, a PFNPROPSHEETUI function, from
  a DLL, a PROPSHEETPAGE, a page handle) before or after a page or as a
  group's first, last or n-th child; pages added while the sheet shows go
  in at their place; a page's handle stands for its group, as some makers'
  pages use it.
- CPSFUNC_SET_RESULT reaches the PFNPROPSHEETUI functions from the page up
  (the program learns OK from it); DELETE_HCOMPROPSHEET, SET_HSTARTPAGE,
  GET_PAGECOUNT, GET_HPSUIPAGES, data blocks, CPSUI's strings and icons,
  page titles, the DMPUB hide bits, IGNORE_CPSUI_PSN_APPLY and
  DO_APPLY_CPSUI.
- COMPROPSHEETUI option lists (OPTITEMs of every option type): on CPSUI's
  treeview page (Advanced, Device Settings), its Layout and Paper/Quality
  pages, or the caller's own dialog templates with controls numbered from
  each type's BegCtrlID; changes go into the OPTITEMs and to the caller's
  callback (whose answer can change or hide options), push buttons and
  extended check boxes and push buttons work, and OK is APPLYNOW, then
  SET_RESULT.
- CPSUI's string table (IDS_CPSUI_*), CommonPropertySheetUIA, and
  Get/SetCPSUIUserData.

Brother's HL-L2310D preferences now open.

Test: test/cpsui-gate.sh with test/cpsui-probe.c, our own (mutants
SG_MUTANT_COMPROP, INSERTPAGE, DATABLOCK, SETRESULT, PAGEGROUP,
CPSUICALLBACK, APPLYRESULT).
